WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.811
Let's set up your company,

2
00:00:01.584 --> 00:00:05.387
so everything Selestial prepares
fits the way you actually work.

3
00:00:06.437 --> 00:00:08.672
Start with your company
name and time zone.

4
00:00:09.119 --> 00:00:12.864
Schedules, availability and
deadlines all run on this clock.

5
00:00:13.914 --> 00:00:15.209
Choose how to begin.

6
00:00:15.203 --> 00:00:17.624
Selestial can read your
website or your records,

7
00:00:17.409 --> 00:00:21.223
but entering the details yourself
is a few short questions.

8
00:00:22.273 --> 00:00:25.681
Add where you're based and the
areas you serve, in your own words.

9
00:00:25.814 --> 00:00:27.492
Then choose who you clean for.

10
00:00:27.753 --> 00:00:31.509
These shape the services and booking
pages Selestial drafts for you.

11
00:00:31.642 --> 00:00:34.319
Nothing is priced or published yet.

12
00:00:35.369 --> 00:00:38.487
Next, how your cleaners work
with you, and roughly how many.

13
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.467
Employees and contractors get different
onboarding and pay rules later on.

14
00:00:44.517 --> 00:00:46.578
Then pick what you'd like help with first.

15
00:00:46.711 --> 00:00:49.864
You can add the others any
time, and setup saves as you go,

16
00:00:49.858 --> 00:00:52.151
so you can finish the rest later.

17
00:00:53.201 --> 00:00:58.397
Two settings change real bookings, so they
live in Settings, under Company profile.

18
00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.412
Add the ZIP codes you serve, and new
bookings are only accepted inside them.

19
00:01:03.766 --> 00:01:05.433
Then set your booking hours.

20
00:01:05.566 --> 00:01:09.009
Each cleaner's own
availability still applies.

21
00:01:10.059 --> 00:01:11.760
That's your company set up.

22
00:01:12.114 --> 00:01:14.535
Next, build your services and pricing,

23
00:01:14.494 --> 00:01:17.693
so customers and your agents
work from real prices.
